%% Kiro-API V3 — elastic worker pool lifecycle
stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Idle: prewarm min_workers
    Idle --> Leased: lease() — fast path (slot free)
    [*] --> Spawning: no idle worker + under max_workers
    Spawning --> Leased: kiro-cli acp started + initialized
    Leased --> Running: session/new + session/prompt
    Running --> Idle: turn done → return to pool
    Running --> Dead: idle/turn timeout, crash, or EOF
    Dead --> [*]: killed (process group) + replaced
    Idle --> Retired: idle_timeout exceeded and total > min_workers
    Retired --> [*]

    note right of Running
        one active turn per worker
        → N workers = N-way parallelism
        (typical ~10, max ~100)
    end note
    note right of Leased
        beyond max_workers requests
        wait in a bounded queue;
        queue full → 503 / 429
    end note
